From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:24:59 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b: Allow power cycle SD
 cards

The boot firmware can leave an inserted SD card in a state that makes the
first Linux enumeration fall back to 50 MHz high-speed mode. Allow the MMC
core to fully cycle the controllable card supply after voltage selection so
UHS-I voltage switching succeeds reliably.

Signed-off-by: Junhao Xie <bigfoot@radxa.com>

(cherry picked from commit 2fce294be52bc2b0dde9674feb493fa7fdd7207f)
[SuperKali: forward-ported from radxa/kernel linux-7.0.11 to Linux 7.2.3]
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-radxa-dragon-q8b.dts
@@ -1412,6 +1412,8 @@ &sdc2 {
 	pinctrl-1 = <&sdc2_sleep_state>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
 
+	full-pwr-cycle;
+
 	vmmc-supply = <&vreg_l9c>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vreg_l6c>;
 
-- 
Armbian

